WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:20.068
"Which road leads to the Wicked Witch of the West?" asked Dorothy politely as they left the Emerald City.

2
00:00:20.069 --> 00:00:23.843
"There is no road," answered the gatekeeper.

3
00:00:23.844 --> 00:00:27.687
"But if you want to find the Witch, it is easy.

4
00:00:27.688 --> 00:00:30.947
Go west, to the land of the Winkies.

5
00:00:30.948 --> 00:00:37.245
There the Witch will find you and make you her slaves."

6
00:00:37.246 --> 00:00:43.274
"We won't become her slaves," said the Scarecrow. "We plan to destroy her."

7
00:00:43.275 --> 00:00:46.818
"Oh, that's different," said the gatekeeper.

8
00:00:46.819 --> 00:00:54.320
"But no one has ever destroyed her before, so I thought she would make you her slaves."

9
00:00:54.321 --> 00:00:59.492
They walked all day. The land became scarier as they went west.

10
00:00:59.493 --> 00:01:05.841
That night Dorothy, Toto, and the Lion rested on the grass while the Scarecrow and the Tin Man stood guard.

11
00:01:05.842 --> 00:01:13.315
From her tower the Wicked Witch of the West used her magic to spy on Dorothy and her friends.

12
00:01:13.316 --> 00:01:16.884
The Witch was angry to see them so near.

13
00:01:16.885 --> 00:01:21.333
She took a silver whistle from around her neck and blew it once.

14
00:01:21.334 --> 00:01:25.615
Soon a pack of evil-looking wolves gathered around her tower.

15
00:01:25.616 --> 00:01:37.492
"Go!" the Witch screamed. "Tear them to pieces!"

16
00:01:37.493 --> 00:01:41.010
"Do you hear that?" asked the Scarecrow.

17
00:01:41.011 --> 00:01:44.810
"Yes, it sounds like wolves," said the Tin Man.

18
00:01:44.811 --> 00:01:48.384
"Get behind me. This is my fight."

19
00:01:48.385 --> 00:01:55.931
The wolves leaped out of the mist, and the Tin Man struck each one down with his ax.

20
00:01:55.932 --> 00:02:01.008
The next morning Dorothy was quite scared to see the pile of dead wolves.

21
00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:05.914
"Don't worry," said the Scarecrow. "We will protect each other."

22
00:02:05.915 --> 00:02:11.950
From her tower the Witch was also looking at the dead wolves, and the scene made her angry.

23
00:02:11.951 --> 00:02:16.923
This time she blew the whistle twice.

24
00:02:16.924 --> 00:02:20.753
Soon a giant flock of crows darkened the sky.

25
00:02:20.754 --> 00:02:27.380
"Go!" screamed the Witch. "Peck out their eyes and tear them to pieces."

26
00:02:27.381 --> 00:02:32.063
The crows immediately flew toward Dorothy and her friends.

27
00:02:32.064 --> 00:02:38.885
The Scarecrow saw the crows coming and ordered, "Lie facedown on the ground! This is my fight."

28
00:02:38.886 --> 00:02:46.992
The crows were scared when they saw the Scarecrow, but the King Crow said, "He is only made of straw."

29
00:02:46.993 --> 00:02:50.667
The King Crow flew at the Scarecrow.

30
00:02:50.668 --> 00:02:55.018
But, one by one, the Scarecrow caught and killed each crow.

31
00:02:55.019 --> 00:02:59.501
When he was done, he said to his friends, "Get up. I have won."

32
00:02:59.502 --> 00:03:04.292
From her tower the Witch watched, and she was furious.

33
00:03:04.293 --> 00:03:09.910
Again she took out her whistle, and this time she blew on it three times.

34
00:03:09.911 --> 00:03:14.245
A swarm of bees appeared.

35
00:03:14.246 --> 00:03:18.979
"Go!" screamed the Witch. "Sting them to death."

36
00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:21.013
The bees flew east.

37
00:03:21.014 --> 00:03:24.366
"Look," said the Tin Man. "Bees!"

38
00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:29.431
"Quick! Cover Dorothy and Lion with my straw," said the Scarecrow.

39
00:03:29.432 --> 00:03:32.643
"The bees won't be able to sting them."

40
00:03:32.644 --> 00:03:46.109
The bees came and found no one but the Tin Man, and of course they could not sting him since he was made of metal.

41
00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:48.588
The Witch was now a little worried.

42
00:03:48.589 --> 00:03:52.428
She had already used many of her most powerful weapons.

43
00:03:52.429 --> 00:03:56.093
She had only one weapon left.

44
00:03:56.094 --> 00:03:59.765
She opened her closet and took out a golden hat.

45
00:03:59.766 --> 00:04:05.719
"This is the last time I can use you," said the Witch.

46
00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:13.041
Then, in a strange voice changed by the magic of the hat, she shouted, "By my command!"

47
00:04:13.042 --> 00:04:16.806
Soon a flock of Winged Monkeys circled her tower.

48
00:04:16.807 --> 00:04:21.615
The largest Monkey flew to her and said, "What do you command?"

49
00:04:21.616 --> 00:04:25.285
"Go and destroy them all!" said the Witch.

50
00:04:25.286 --> 00:04:31.389
"Except the Lion. I want to make him my pet."

51
00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:34.248
The Winged Monkeys did as she commanded.

52
00:04:34.249 --> 00:04:40.199
One group grabbed the Tin Man, carried him high into the sky, and dropped him onto some rocks.

53
00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:48.777
Another group pulled the straw out of the Scarecrow, scattered it, and then placed his clothes in the tallest tree.

54
00:04:48.778 --> 00:04:55.336
A third group tackled the Lion, tied him with ropes, and brought him to the Witch.

55
00:04:55.337 --> 00:04:57.797
But they did not harm Dorothy.

56
00:04:57.798 --> 00:05:01.531
"We cannot harm the girl," said the largest Monkey.

57
00:05:01.532 --> 00:05:04.919
"Bring her to the Witch–she will deal with her."

58
00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:14.567
The Monkeys took Dorothy to the Witch's tower and then disappeared.
